+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling One Stays Out
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declared changing or cancelling a booked visit out of scope, and the [2026-08-08 non-goal ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) confirmed the row as a deliberate product decision rather than a survey artifact. That ADR set the condition for reopening it: narrowing the row later is a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR, and no request reopens the row by implication.
+
+The owner has now made that decision (2026-08-28). A visit's date and description can be entered wrongly, and the sample offers no way back — every other record in it can be corrected forward, which makes the visit the one exception.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the correction gap is inconsistent with the forward-only correction the owner and pet flows already demonstrate.
+2. **Open the whole row** — correction and cancellation together. Rejected: cancellation is what carries the lifecycle state the 2026-08-08 rationale declined. Correction carries none: it replaces two field values on an existing record.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, recorded as [`REQ-VIS-003`](../prd.md#req-vis-003). NG-5 now covers cancelling a booked visit and nothing else. NG-4 is untouched: deleting a visit stays out of scope.
+
+The first round of the capability ships with no entry point on the owner's record — the correction page is reached by its own address. That is a deferred item, not a declined one, and the PRD's Deferred section records it; a follow-up request adds the link.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Visits join owners and pets as records the sample corrects forward. The deletion boundary is unchanged, and no visit lifecycle state is introduced.
+- A correction obeys the same validation as a booking, which bars correcting a visit whose date has already passed. Whether that is intended is an open question against `REQ-VIS-003`.
+- The capability is unreachable by navigation until the deferred link ships, so it is exercised by address and by test only.
+- Narrowing NG-5 again, or reopening cancellation, is a further owner decision with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row and the preamble that dates the narrowing.
+- [PRD Deferred](../prd.md#deferred) — the withheld link from an owner's record.
+- [`REQ-VIS-003`](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the capability this narrowing admits.
